<title>GERMANY: DTB says to start dlr/mark options trade on Monday.</title>
<headline>DTB says to start dlr/mark options trade on Monday.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German futures and options exchange, Deutsche Terminboerse (DTB), said it will start trade in dollar/mark options on Monday, in line with its announced plans to launch such a contract in January.</p>
<p>The underlying volume for the option is $50,000. The contracts will have a maturity of up to 12 months.</p>
<p>Market-making will initially be carried out by 14 institutions in Germany and abroad, but this can be expanded if new products are added, the German bourse said.</p>
<p>The dollar/mark option is aimed at both private and institutional investors.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
